{
  "title": "Aamal of the Last Ten Nights of Ramazan",
  "data": "Dua A'udhu bi-Jalali Wajhik\nFrom the 21st night on, recite these duas on each of the last ten nights of Ramazan.\nاَعُوْذُ بِجَلَالِ وَجْهِكَ الْكَرِيْمِ اَنْ يَنْقَضِيَ عَنِّي شَهْرُ رَمَضَانَ\nA'OODHU BIJALAALI WAJHIKAL KAREEMI AN YANQADIYA A'NNEE SHAHRU RAMADAAN\nI seek the protection of the Majesty of Your Honorable Face against that the month of Ramadan elapses\nاَوْ يَطْلُعَ الْفَجْرُ مِنْ لَيْلَتِيْ هٰذِهِ وَلَكَ قِبَلِيْ ذَنْبٌ اَوْ تَبِعَةٌ تُعَذِّبُنِيْ عَلَيْهِ\nAW YATLU'AL FAJRU MIN LAYLATEE HAADHIHEE WA LAKA QIBALEE DHANBUN AW TABI'ATUN TU'ADHDHIBUNEE A'LAYH\nor dawn puts an end to this night but there is still an offense or a sin for which I am still liable and for which You will punish me.",
  "tabs": [
    "Allahumma Addi Anna\nAfter the obligatory and nafilah prayers, recite:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اَدِّ عَنَّا حَقَّ مَا مَضٰى مِنْ شَهْرِ رَمَضَانَ وَاغْفِرْ لَنَا تَقْصِيْرَنَا فِيْهِ\nALLAAHUMMA ADDI A'NNAA HAQQA MAA MADAA MIN SHAHRI RAMADAANA WAGHFIR LANAA TAQSEERANAA FEEH\nO Allah, (please) help us fulfill the right of the past days of the month of Ramadan, forgive us our shortcoming during it\nوَتَسَلَّمْهُ مِنَّا مَقْبُوْلًا، وَلَا تُؤَاخِذْنَا بِاِسْرَافِنَا عَلٰى اَنْفُسِنَا\nWA TASALLAMHU MINNAA MAQBOOLAN WA LAA TU'AAKHIDHNAA BI-ISRAAFINAA A'LAA ANFUSINAA\nreceive it from us with acceptance, do not blame us for our extravagance in our affairs\nوَاجْعَلْنَا مِنَ الْمَرْحُوْمِيْنَ وَلَا تَجْعَلْنَا مِنَ الْمَحْرُوْمِيْنَ\nWAJ'ALNAA MINAL MARHOOMEENA WA LAA TAJ'ALNAA MINAL MAHROOMEEN\ninclude us with those upon whom mercy is had, and do not include us with those deprived (of the awards of Ramadan).",
    "Dua Allahumma Innaka Qulta\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنَّكَ قُلْتَ فِيْ كِتَابِكَ الْمُنْزَلِ شَهْرُ رَمَضَانَ الَّذِيْ اُنْزِلَ فِيْهِ الْقُرْاٰنُ هُدًى لِلنَّاسِ وَبَيِّنَاتٍ مِنَ الْهُدٰى وَالْفُرْقَانِ\nALLAAHUMMA INNAKA QULTA FEE KITAABIKAL MUNZALI SHAHRU RAMADAANAL LADHEE UNZILA FEEHIL QUR'AANU HUDAN LIN NAASI WA BAYYINAATIN MINAL HUDAA WAL FURQAAN\nO Allah, You have said in Your revealed Book: “The month of Ramadan is that in which the Qur'an was revealed, a guidance to men and clear proofs of the guidance and the distinction.”\nفَعَظَّمْتَ حُرْمَةَ شَهْرِ رَمَضَانَ بِمَا اَنْزَلْتَ فِيْهِ مِنَ الْقُرْاٰنِ، وَخَصَصْتَهٗ بِلَيْلَةِ الْقَدْرِ وَجَعَلْتَهَا خَيْرًا مِنْ اَلْفِ شَهْرٍ\nFA'AZZAMTA HURMATA SHAHRI RAMADAANA BIMAA ANZALTA FEEHI MINAL QUR'AANI WA KHASASTAHOO BILAYLATIL QADRI WA JA'ALTAHAA KHAYRAN MIN ALFI SHAHR\nYou have thus rendered great the sanctity of this month of Ramadan, because You revealed the Qur'an in it, decided the Destiny Night to be in this month exclusively, and made it better than one thousand months.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ وَهٰذِهِ اَيَّامُ شَهْرِ رَمَضَانَ قَدِ انْقَضَتْ، وَلَيَالِيْهِ قَدْ تَصَرَّمَتْ\nALLAAHUMMA WA HAADHIHEE AYYAAMU SHAHRI RAMADAANA QADIN QADAT WA LAYAALEEHI QAD TASARRAMAT\nO Allah, the days of the month of Ramadan are elapsing, its nights are also elapsing\nوَقَدْ صِرْتُ يَا اِلٰهِيْ مِنْهُ اِلٰى مَا اَنْتَ اَعْلَمُ بِهٖ مِنِّي وَاَحْصٰى لِعَدَدِهٖ مِنَ الْخَلْقِ اَجْمَعِيْنَ\nWA QAD SIRTU YAA ILAAHEE MINHU ILAA MAA ANTA A'LAMU BIHEE MINNEE WA AHSAA LI-A'DADIHEE MINAL KHALQI AJMA'EEN\nwhile I have become in the state that You, O my God, know better than I do, and You can count it more precisely than all the created beings.\nفَاَسْاَلُكَ بِمَا سَاَلَكَ بِهٖ مَلَآئِكَتُكَ الْمُقَرَّبُوْنَ وَاَنْبِيَآؤُكَ الْمُرْسَلُوْنَ، وَعِبَادُكَ الصَّالِحُوْنَ\nFA-AS'ALUKA BIMAA SA'ALAKA BIHEE MALAA'IKATUKAL MUQARRABOONA WA ANBIYAA'UKAL MURSALOONA WA I'BAADUKAS SAALIHOON\nSo, I beseech You in the name of that by which Your favorite angels, Your missioned Prophets, and Your righteous servants have besought You\nاَنْ تُصَلِّيَ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ وَاَنْ تَفُكَّ رَقَبَتِيْ مِنَ النَّارِ، وَتُدْخِلَنِيْ الْجَنَّةَ بِرَحْمَتِكَ\nAN TUSALLIYA A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMADIN WA AN TAFUKKA RAQABATEE MINAN NAARI WA TUDKHILANIL JANNATA BIRAHMATIK\nto bless Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad, release me from Hellfire, allow me to enter Paradise by Your mercy\nوَاَنْ تَتَفَضَّلَ عَلَيَّ بِعَفْوِكَ وَكَرَمِكَ وَتَتَقَبَّلَ تَقَرُّبِيْ وَتَسْتَجِيْبَ دُعَآئِيْ\nWA AN TATAFADDALA A'LAYYA BI-A'FWIKA WA KARAMIKA WA TATAQABBALA TAQARRUBEE WA TASTAJEEBA DU'AA'EE\nconfer upon me with Your pardon and Your generosity, accept my seeking of nearness to You, respond to my prayer\nوَتَمُنَّ عَلَيَّ بِالْاَمْنِ يَوْمَ الْخَوْفِ مِنْ كُلِّ هَوْلٍ اَعْدَدْتَهٗ لِيَوْمِ الْقِيَامَةِ\nWA TAMUNNA A'LAYYA BIL AMNI YAWMAL KHAWFI MIN KULLI HAWLIN A'DADTAHOO LIYAWMIL QIYAAMAH\nand bestow upon me with security on the Day of Dread against all the horrors that You have prepared for the Resurrection Day.\nاِلٰهِيْ وَاَعُوْذُ بِوَجْهِكَ الْكَرِيْمِ، وَبِجَلَالِكَ الْعَظِيْمِ اَنْ يَنْقَضِيَ اَيَّامُ شَهْرِ رَمَضَانَ وَلَيَالِيْهِ وَلَكَ قِبَلِيْ تَبِعَةٌ اَوْ ذَنْبٌ تُؤَاخِذُنِيْ بِهٖ\nILAAHEE WA A'OODHU BIWAJHIKAL KAREEMI WA BIJALAALIKAL A'ZEEMI AN YANQADIYA AYYAAMU SHAHRI RAMADAANA WA LAYAALEEHI WA LAKA QIBALEE TABI'ATUN AW DHANBUN TU'AAKHIDHUNEE BIH\nO my God, I seek the protection of Your Noble Face and Your Great Majesty against that the days and nights of the month of Ramadan elapse while there is still a sin or an offense for which You may punish me\nاَوْ خَطِيْئَةٌ تُرِيْدُ اَنْ تَقْتَصَّهَا مِنِّيْ لَمْ تَغْفِرْهَا لِيْ\nAW KHATEE'ATUN TUREEDU AN TAQTASSAHAA MINNEE LAM TAGHFIRHAA LEE\nor a wrongdoing for which You want to chastise me and You have not yet forgiven them for me.\nسَيِّدِيْ سَيِّدِيْ سَيِّدِيْ\nSAYYIDEE SAYYIDEE SAYYIDEE\nO my Master! O my Master! O my Master!\nاَسْاَلُكَ يَا لَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اَنْتَ اِذْ لَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اَنْتَ\nAS'ALUKA YAA LAA ILAAHA ILLAA ANTA IDH LAA ILAAHA ILLAA ANT\nI beseech You, O He save Whom there is no god, since there is indeed no god save You\nاِنْ كُنْتَ رَضِيْتَ عَنِّي فِيْ هٰذَا الشَّهْرِ فَازْدَدْ عَنِّيْ رِضًا\nIN KUNTA RADEETA A'NNEE FEE HAADHASH SHAHRI FAZDAD A'NNEE RIDAA\nif You have been pleased with me in this month, then (please) increase Your satisfaction with me\nوَاِنْ لَمْ تَكُنْ رَضِيْتَ عَنِّي فَمِنَ الْاٰنَ فَارْضَ عَنِّيْ\nWA IN LAM TAKUN RADEETA A'NNEE FAMINAL AANA FARDA A'NNEE\nbut if You have not been pleased with me, then (please) be satisfied with me from this moment.\nيَا اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِيْنَ، يَا اَللهُ يَا اَحَدُ يَا صَمَدُ\nYAA ARHAMAR RAAHIMEENA YAA ALLAAHU YAA AHADU YAA SAMAD\nO most Merciful of all those who show mercy! O Allah! O One and Only! O Besought of all!\nيَا مَنْ لَمْ يَلِدْ وَلَمْ يُوْلَدْ وَلَمْ يَكُنْ لَهٗ كُفُوًا اَحَدٌ\nYAA MAN LAM YALID WA LAM YOOLAD WA LAM YAKUN LAHOO KUFUWAN AHAD\nO He Who begets not, nor is He begotten, and none is like Him!",
    "Dua Ya Mulayyin al-Hadid\nRecite as many times as you can:\nيَا مُلَيِّنَ الْحَدِيْدِ لِدَاوُدَ عَلَيْهِ السَّلَامُ\nYAA MULAYYINAL HADEEDI LIDAAWUDA A'LAYHIS SALAAM\nO He Who made the iron pliant for (Prophet) David, peace be upon him!\nيَا كَاشِفَ الضُّرِّ وَالْكُرَبِ الْعِظَامِ عَنْ اَيُّوْبَ عَلَيْهِ السَّلَامُ\nYAA KAASHIFAD DURRI WAL KURABIL I'ZAAMI A'N AYYOOBA A'LAYHIS SALAAM\nO He Who took off the harm and calamity that afflict (Prophet) Job, peace be upon him!\nاَيْ مُفَرِّجَ هَمِّ يَعْقُوْبَ عَلَيْهِ السَّلَامُ\nAY MUFARRIJA HAMMI YA'QOOBA A'LAYHIS SALAAM\nO He Who relieved the sorrow of (Prophet) Jacob, peace be upon him!\nاَيْ مُنَفِّسَ غَمِّ يُوْسُفَ عَلَيْهِ السَّلَامُ\nAY MUNAFFISA GHAMMI YOOSUFA A'LAYHIS SALAAM\nO He Who removed the grief of (Prophet) Joseph, peace be upon him!\nصَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ كَمَا اَنْتَ اَهْلُهٗ اَنْ تُصَلِّيَ عَلَيْهِمْ اَجْمَعِيْنَ\nSALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMADIN KAMAA ANTA AHLUHOO AN TUSALLIYA A'LAYHIM AJMA'EEN\n(Please do) send blessings to Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad as exactly as You are worth blessing them all\nوَافْعَلْ بِيْ مَا اَنْتَ اَهْلُهٗ وَلَا تَفْعَلْ بِيْ مَا اَنَا اَهْلُهٗ\nWAF'AL BEE MAA ANTA AHLUHOO WA LAA TAF'AL BEE MAA ANAA AHLUH\ndo to me that which befits You, and do not do to me that which I deserve.",
    "21st Night: Ya Mulij al-Layl\nOn the 21st night, recite:\nيَا مُوْلِجَ اللَّيْلِ فِي النَّهَارِ، وَمُوْلِجَ النَّهَارِ فِي اللَّيْلِ\nYAA MOOLIJAL LAYLI FIN NAHAARI WA MOOLIJAN NAHAARI FIL LAYL\nO He Who causes the night to enter into the day, causes the day to enter into the night\nوَمُخْرِجَ الْحَيِّ مِنَ الْمَيِّتِ، وَمُخْرِجَ الْمَيِّتِ مِنَ الْحَيِّ\nWA MUKHRIJAL HAYYI MINAL MAYYITI WA MUKHRIJAL MAYYITI MINAL HAYY\nbrings forth the living from the dead, and brings forth the dead from the living!\nيَا رَازِقَ مَنْ يَشَاۤءُ بِغَيْرِ حِسَابٍ\nYAA RAAZIQA MAN YASHAA'U BIGHAYRI HISAAB\nO He Who gives sustenance to whomever He please without measure!\nيَا اَللهُ يَا رَحْمٰنُ، يَا اَللهُ يَا رَحِيْمُ، يَا اَللهُ يَا اَللهُ يَا اَللهُ\nYAA ALLAAHU YAA RAHMAANU YAA ALLAAHU YAA RAHEEMU YAA ALLAAHU YAA ALLAAHU YAA ALLAAH\nO Allah! O All-beneficent! O Allah! O All-merciful! O Allah! O Allah! O Allah!\nلَكَ الْاَسْمَاۤءُ الْحُسْنٰى، وَالْاَمْثَالُ الْعُلْيَا، وَالْكِبْرِيَاۤءُ وَالْاٰلَاۤءُ\nLAKAL ASMAA'UL HUSNAA WAL AMTHAALUL U'LYAA WAL KIBRIYAA'U WAL AALAA'\nTo You are the Most Excellent Names, the most elevated examples, greatness, and bounties.\nاَسْاَلُكَ اَنْ تُصَلِّيَ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nAS'ALUKA AN TUSALLIYA A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMAD\nI beseech You to bless Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad\nوَاَنْ تَجْعَلَ اسْمِيْ فِيْ هٰذِهِ اللَّيْلَةِ فِي السُّعَدَاۤءِ، وَرُوْحِيْ مَعَ الشُّهَدَاۤءِ\nWA AN TAJ'ALAS MEE FEE HAADHIHIL LAYLATI FIS SU'ADAA'I WA ROOHEE MA'ASH SHUHADAA'\ninclude my name with the list of the happiest ones, add my soul to the martyrs\nوَاِحْسَانِيْ فِي عِلِّيِّيْنَ، وَاِسَآئَتِيْ مَغْفُوْرَةً\nWA IHSAANEE FEE I'LLIYYEENA WA ISAA'ATEE MAGHFOORAH\nrecord my good deeds in the most exalted rank, decide my offense to be forgiven\nوَاَنْ تَهَبَ لِيْ يَقِيْنًا تُبَاشِرُ بِهٖ قَلْبِيْ، وَاِيْمَانًا يُذْهِبُ الشَّكَّ عَنِّي\nWA AN TAHABA LEE YAQEENAN TUBAASHIRU BIHEE QALBEE WA EEMAANAN YUDH-HIBUSH SHAKKA A'NNEE\ngrant me certitude that fills in my heart and faith that removes doubt from me\nوَتُرْضِيَنِيْ بِمَا قَسَمْتَ لِي\nWA TURDIYANEE BIMAA QASAMTA LEE\nmake me feel satisfied with that which You decide for me\nوَاٰتِنَا فِي الدُّنْيَا حَسَنَةً، وَفِي الْاٰخِرَةِ حَسَنَةً، وَقِنَا عَذَابَ النَّارِ الْحَرِيْقِ\nWA AATINAA FID DUNYAA HASANATAN WA FIL AAKHIRATI HASANATAN WA QINAA A'DHAABAN NAARIL HAREEQ\ngrant us reward in this world and reward in the Hereafter, save us from the torment of the burning Fire\nوَارْزُقْنِيْ فِيْهَا ذِكْرَكَ وَشُكْرَكَ وَالرَّغْبَةَ اِلَيْكَ، وَالْاِنَابَةَ وَالتَّوْفِيْقَ لِمَا وَفَّقْتَ لَهٗ مُحَمَّدًا وَاٰلَ مُحَمَّدٍ عَلَيْهِ وَعَلَيْهِمُ السَّلَامُ\nWARZUQNEE FEEHAA DHIKRAKA WA SHUKRAKA WAR RAGHBATA ILAYKA WAL INAABATA WAT TAWFEEQA LIMAA WAFFAQTA LAHOO MUHAMMADAN WA AALA MUHAMMADIN A'LAYHI WA A'LAYHIMUS SALAAM\nand confer upon us at this night Your mentioning, thanking You, desiring for You, turning to You, and success to that to which You led Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad, peace be upon him and them."
  ],
  "merits": "Dua A'udhu bi-Jalali Wajhik: In al-Kafi, Shaykh al-Kulayni has reported Imam Ja'far al-Sadiq (a.s.) as saying: At the last ten nights of Ramadan, you may say this supplicatory prayer.\n\nAllahumma Addi Anna: As a footnote in al-Balad al-Amin, al-Kaf'ami has mentioned that Imam Ja'far al-Sadiq (a.s.) used to say this supplicatory prayer at each of the last ten nights of Ramadan after the obligatory and supererogatory (mustahab / nafilah) prayers. He adds that Almighty Allah will forgive one who says this supplicatory prayer all the sins that he has committed in the past days of Ramadan and will protect him against sinning in the rest of it.\n\nDua Allahumma Innaka Qulta: In Iqbal al-A'mal, Sayyid Ibn Tawus has narrated on the authority of Ibn Abi-'Umayr on the authority of Murazim that Imam Ja'far al-Sadiq (a.s.) used to say this supplicatory prayer at each of the last ten nights of Ramadan.\n\n21st Night: Ya Mulij al-Layl: Shaykh al-Kulayni, in al-Kafi, has narrated, with a complete chain of authority, that this supplicatory prayer, which is also narrated in al-Muqni'ah and al-Misbah yet with an interruption in the chain of authority, should be said at the twenty-first night of Ramadan."
}
